WEBVTT

00:00:01.048 --> 00:00:12.926
Yes, I embraced tenderness and devotion
sou itooshisa to kizuna wo daita

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:18.632
Floating in unending space
hatenaki umi ni ukabu

00:00:18.632 --> 00:00:25.561
On this small planet
chiisa na hoshi de

00:00:26.073 --> 00:00:37.109
When I feel your warmth next to me
anata no nukumori wo soba ni kanjiru toki

00:00:37.284 --> 00:00:43.223
I understand the burden
inochi no omosa to

00:00:43.223 --> 00:00:50.629
And the transience of life
hakanasa wo shiru no

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:58.438
Nights of sorrowful wandering
mayoinageku yoru mo

00:00:58.438 --> 00:01:05.312
And tearful mornings
namida no asa mo

00:01:05.312 --> 00:01:10.917
I believe in tomorrow
ashita wo shinjiru kara

00:01:10.917 --> 00:01:17.190
So I can make it through
koeteyukeru no

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:25.620
To the continuation of the dream
yume no tsuzuki he

00:01:44.518 --> 00:01:49.353
1901 SWEDEN

00:01:59.332 --> 00:02:02.702
I see, thanks to your explanation...

00:02:02.702 --> 00:02:04.604
We now understand how the
discovery of x-rays came about...

00:02:04.604 --> 00:02:05.372
WANDERING MEMORIES
We now understand how the
discovery of x-rays came about...

00:02:05.372 --> 00:02:07.007
WANDERING MEMORIES
...and what was involved.

00:02:07.007 --> 00:02:07.140
WANDERING MEMORIES

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:09.476
WANDERING MEMORIES
By the way, Professor Rugen...

00:02:09.576 --> 00:02:12.312
I've heard that when you were in school...

00:02:12.312 --> 00:02:16.283
physics and mathematics were
not your best subjects.

00:02:16.283 --> 00:02:19.453
However, you've gone on
to become the physicist...

00:02:19.453 --> 00:02:21.887
...who has made the discovery
of the century.

00:02:21.988 --> 00:02:26.152
What caused this change
in the direction of your life?

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:30.662
Indeed, after I graduated from
engineering school...

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:33.961
I seriously thought of becoming
a mechanical engineer.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.992
I've heard that you were
fond of steam engines.

00:02:41.708 --> 00:02:45.769
I don't know if it's really
the reason for the change...

00:02:48.682 --> 00:02:51.651
It was around the time
I had just turned twenty five.

00:02:51.818 --> 00:02:55.151
On a day when I was thinking
about going back to Holland,

00:02:55.188 --> 00:02:58.487
I happened to have
a very mysterious day.

00:03:05.165 --> 00:03:07.326
Mysterious...

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:17.135
White hair shining like silver...

00:03:17.711 --> 00:03:21.442
Serene, sorrowful blue eyes...

00:03:23.083 --> 00:03:25.779
A little girl.

00:03:40.967 --> 00:03:44.198
When she looked at me,

00:03:44.337 --> 00:03:49.502
I don't know what it was exactly
but something compelled me...

00:03:49.643 --> 00:03:52.009
to walk with her.

00:03:52.879 --> 00:03:55.982
Without saying a word, in silence,

00:03:55.982 --> 00:03:59.352
just knowing that girl was beside me.

00:03:59.352 --> 00:04:01.912
A very mysterious day...

00:04:05.292 --> 00:04:08.921
-That was...
-Palza.

00:04:09.329 --> 00:04:14.334
Oh, I see.
If you were 25 years old,

00:04:14.334 --> 00:04:16.436
...then soon after that you became
Professor Qunto's assistant...

00:04:16.436 --> 00:04:18.563
...at the Weltzburg University.

00:04:18.605 --> 00:04:20.766
The professor appears
to be getting tired.

00:04:20.807 --> 00:04:23.970
I think it's about time we
end the press conference.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:27.111
The chance discovery of x-rays...

00:04:28.081 --> 00:04:31.244
Aghi, do you think it was
really just chance?

00:04:31.384 --> 00:04:34.046
It could be... I really don't know.

00:04:34.087 --> 00:04:38.058
But now that this has happened, we
have to be more careful from now on.

00:04:38.058 --> 00:04:40.860
It's almost time for us
to go meet Hesma.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:45.763
-Is that artist really Tina?
-We'll know when we talk to Hesma.

00:04:46.366 --> 00:04:48.391
-Mel, let's go.
-Okay!

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:08.217
Mel?

00:05:11.825 --> 00:05:13.190
Mel!

00:05:18.131 --> 00:05:20.691
S-Soreto?

00:05:25.605 --> 00:05:28.438
-Hesma!
-It's been confirmed!

00:05:28.541 --> 00:05:30.532
Let's go.

00:05:31.144 --> 00:05:34.944
2012 CHIKAO. HOME FOR CHILDREN

00:07:12.812 --> 00:07:15.576
There have been wars
and countless conflicts,

00:07:15.682 --> 00:07:17.707
but this castle still stands.

00:07:17.751 --> 00:07:21.243
We've come here and done this
same thing more than 20 times.

00:07:22.255 --> 00:07:25.792
It's intuition. Besides,
in any country you go to...

00:07:25.792 --> 00:07:28.590
...churches and temples
are built to last.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:34.195
Even this place is a church that
was converted into a library.

00:07:35.802 --> 00:07:37.827
Found it.

00:07:47.514 --> 00:07:50.915
The record of our memories,
left behind in the last year.

00:07:51.651 --> 00:07:53.676
Aghi.

00:07:56.990 --> 00:08:00.084
Hasmodye. Here, Tarlant.

00:08:00.226 --> 00:08:02.524
I don't really need it though.

00:08:03.363 --> 00:08:07.390
Even without using this,
I am always myself.

00:08:11.771 --> 00:08:13.830
Soreto's.

00:08:14.741 --> 00:08:18.074
And Palza and Mel's.

00:08:22.482 --> 00:08:25.645
If only we could have given
this to Mel a little earlier,

00:08:25.952 --> 00:08:29.786
we might have been able
to reinforce her memories.

00:08:30.323 --> 00:08:34.123
Her will was weak.
To forget herself like that.

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:36.490
You shouldn't say things like that.

00:08:38.531 --> 00:08:41.329
It's them! They're here!

00:11:30.436 --> 00:11:33.269
Hasmodye! Hasmodye!

00:11:34.874 --> 00:11:38.435
Don't be afraid, Hasmodye.
They'll see into your heart.

00:11:38.578 --> 00:11:41.979
They are always looking for us.

00:11:46.386 --> 00:11:49.719
This is the last one
that mentions Serafine.

00:11:50.523 --> 00:11:54.193
-She was a beautiful woman.
-Died in 1901.

00:11:54.193 --> 00:11:56.195
If we're right about the
100 year interval,

00:11:56.195 --> 00:11:58.220
she should be 11 years old like us.

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:05.200
It's already been 11 years...
11 years since we arrived here.

00:12:06.272 --> 00:12:09.469
The old man in the hospital...
He was an art dealer.

00:12:09.509 --> 00:12:11.500
Soreto.

00:12:13.813 --> 00:12:16.907
Someday, somewhere,
we might meet again.

00:12:18.851 --> 00:12:21.454
Let's go back to Clairmont
and search there again.

00:12:21.454 --> 00:12:23.423
I was five when we gathered together,

00:12:23.423 --> 00:12:25.482
and we've gone there
more than ten times.

00:12:25.591 --> 00:12:28.561
We have to be careful,
he's out there somewhere.

00:12:28.561 --> 00:12:32.258
You saw how Dumas looked.
He's hardly aged at all.

00:12:32.732 --> 00:12:35.935
Even so, we can't just keep running.

00:12:35.935 --> 00:12:39.837
He saw those paintings then too.
We have to hurry.

00:12:43.643 --> 00:12:45.702
Are we...

00:12:47.647 --> 00:12:50.047
...monsters?

00:12:50.983 --> 00:12:52.919
Just one more year.
No,

00:12:52.919 --> 00:12:58.691
we don't know for sure if
we even have twelve years.

00:12:58.691 --> 00:13:01.785
With the approach of our twelfth year,
our memories will start to fade rapidly.

00:13:01.861 --> 00:13:04.330
And then confusion and insecurity...

00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:06.821
...will cause us to suddenly
cease to be ourselves.

00:13:07.166 --> 00:13:09.225
We must hurry...

00:13:56.415 --> 00:13:59.873
Good morning.
Look, it's the key to the back door.

00:14:00.219 --> 00:14:02.312
-Let's go.
-Yes.

00:14:11.130 --> 00:14:14.200
Hey, you forgot your clipboard.

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:16.964
Man, I'm tired.

00:14:20.907 --> 00:14:22.966
All right then.

00:14:29.415 --> 00:14:31.576
We're finally leaving!

00:14:55.875 --> 00:14:59.178
What's up, Thoma? You're putting more
effort than usual into it today.

00:14:59.178 --> 00:15:02.773
You're the one who told me to be
more serious about it, Dad!

00:15:09.822 --> 00:15:12.291
That's right.
But depending on strength...

00:15:12.291 --> 00:15:14.851
...is just superficial.
It weakens your spirit.

00:15:14.927 --> 00:15:17.020
Leaving you open
to attack, Thoma!

00:15:20.199 --> 00:15:21.000
Damn!

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:23.525
Thoma, I'm leaving.

00:15:29.675 --> 00:15:31.700
Honey!

00:15:33.679 --> 00:15:36.882
Honey! Oh no!
You knocked him out!

00:15:36.882 --> 00:15:40.318
-Oh, shoot!
-Honey! Honey!

00:15:43.356 --> 00:15:47.526
Director! It looks like they did sneak out
on the early morning boat to Natsuna!

00:15:47.526 --> 00:15:50.429
Yesterday and again today!
What were you people doing?!

00:15:50.429 --> 00:15:51.998
How can you let children
make fools of you?

00:15:51.998 --> 00:15:53.659
Go to Natsuna and
capture them immediately!

00:15:53.699 --> 00:15:55.690
Understood!

00:16:04.477 --> 00:16:07.747
There's such a nice pier here,
but it never gets used.

00:16:07.747 --> 00:16:10.307
Well, tourists never come here
so the boats don't either.

00:16:10.349 --> 00:16:13.182
There's nothing on this island.

00:16:13.352 --> 00:16:16.753
This temple has 200 years
of history behind it.

00:16:16.822 --> 00:16:19.382
Thoma, you'll be its next caretaker.
You know that, don't you?

00:16:20.259 --> 00:16:23.387
Mom, your makeup makes
you look like a witch.

00:16:23.462 --> 00:16:26.232
Well, looking like this is
appropriate for fortunetelling.

00:16:26.232 --> 00:16:28.701
Dad's always complaining about it.

00:16:28.701 --> 00:16:30.403
He's stubborn and doesn't
understand business.

00:16:30.403 --> 00:16:32.701
Because he's the nervous type.

00:16:34.106 --> 00:16:37.439
By the way, Thoma, you were making
some strange noises this morning.

00:16:37.476 --> 00:16:39.341
Did you have another dream?

00:16:40.046 --> 00:16:42.105
I don't know.

00:17:05.137 --> 00:17:07.973
Hey, Mom.
The children's home...

00:17:07.973 --> 00:17:10.134
Do you think maybe it isn't any fun?

00:17:10.176 --> 00:17:11.711
What a thing to ask!

00:17:11.711 --> 00:17:15.078
It's not an amusement park
so I doubt it's much fun.

00:17:15.214 --> 00:17:17.650
Children go there for
a lot of different reasons.

00:17:17.650 --> 00:17:21.142
But if they have good instructors
it shouldn't be that bad.

00:17:23.122 --> 00:17:25.556
You really should be
going to school too.

00:17:25.591 --> 00:17:28.992
You don't have to worry about me
studying. Dad is teaching me.

00:17:29.061 --> 00:17:31.427
But you could make friends at school.

00:17:35.267 --> 00:17:37.360
Friends?

00:17:41.974 --> 00:17:46.104
Okay, thank you. Pick me
up at the usual time.

00:17:52.251 --> 00:17:56.122
-What's the matter, Thoma?
-Nothing! I gotcha!

00:17:56.122 --> 00:17:58.317
Have a safe trip home.

00:18:25.551 --> 00:18:28.816
As far as we can go.
Two children.

00:18:29.722 --> 00:18:31.713
Here!

00:19:02.755 --> 00:19:05.280
She did run away again!

00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:12.196
Hey, you! If you stay here
you'll be spotted.

00:19:12.431 --> 00:19:14.899
-What?!
-Oops!

00:19:16.368 --> 00:19:18.836
Sorry. Thought you were someone else.

00:19:20.005 --> 00:19:22.701
What's wrong with you?
How rude!

00:19:23.709 --> 00:19:25.904
Geez! What's with her?!

00:19:31.050 --> 00:19:33.177
Sorry! You okay?

00:19:36.088 --> 00:19:38.113
Tarlant.

00:19:40.659 --> 00:19:43.127
Huh?

00:19:48.167 --> 00:19:50.727
What's the matter with them?

00:19:50.970 --> 00:19:54.633
You could at least
say excuse me!

00:19:57.510 --> 00:19:59.512
The train bound for Ayuta via Claremont...

00:19:59.512 --> 00:20:02.379
...on the Western Mainland
will be departing shortly.

00:20:02.515 --> 00:20:04.550
Please board the train and
await departure.

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:06.643
We got on!

00:20:07.453 --> 00:20:09.751
I wonder how far
we'll be able to go.

00:20:10.389 --> 00:20:13.222
From now on, we'll always be together.

00:20:22.635 --> 00:20:24.933
Oh, it's a horse!

00:21:18.157 --> 00:21:20.387
Guess they're not here.

00:21:32.571 --> 00:21:34.562
Huh?

00:21:39.945 --> 00:21:44.541
I am lost and burning
in the desert of human life.

00:21:45.217 --> 00:21:49.551
And I groan under the
heavy burden I carry.

00:21:50.756 --> 00:21:55.159
But somewhere, there is an
almost forgotten blossoming,

00:21:55.394 --> 00:22:00.229
in a garden of cool shadows.
I know it.

00:22:01.300 --> 00:22:05.760
However, in a place so far away
it seems like dream,

00:22:05.804 --> 00:22:09.763
a resting place is waiting.
I know it.

00:22:10.175 --> 00:22:12.878
My soul will once again have a home,

00:22:12.878 --> 00:22:17.542
a place where rest and
night and stars are waiting...

00:22:35.567 --> 00:22:45.374
At the bottom of the deep, clear sea
fukaku fukaku sukitooru umi no soko ni

00:22:45.644 --> 00:22:55.487
A small flower is resting
chiisana hana madoronderu

00:22:55.487 --> 00:23:00.220
The melody of a gentle wind
amayaka na kaze no shirabe

00:23:00.259 --> 00:23:05.094
Passes through a rainbow
niji wo kuguri

00:23:05.497 --> 00:23:14.633
The fish are playing in the sky
sakanatachi wa sora ni asobu

00:23:14.740 --> 00:23:19.812
Everyone plays the music of love
dare mo ga ai wo kanaderu

00:23:19.812 --> 00:23:25.084
A warm light came down
atatakana hikari futteta

00:23:25.084 --> 00:23:29.487
(A gaze) That gaze
(manazashi wa) sono manazashi wa

00:23:29.521 --> 00:23:33.826
Is unbound and becomes full
hodokete michiteku

00:23:33.826 --> 00:23:38.695
Embraced by water
mizu ni dakare
